   "text": "If Sam keeps getting up every time, the evening changes shape."
  },
  {
   "start": 4.8,
   "end": 10.25,
   "text": "He never fully sits. He watches ten minutes, pauses, checks something, comes back."
  },
  {
   "start": 10.3,
   "end": 15.05,
   "text": "The episode he waited all day for turns into background noise."
  },
  {
   "start": 15.1,
   "end": 22.55,
   "text": "And the lesson he learns is a bad one: *rest* is only safe after the work is done."
  },
  {
   "start": 22.6,
   "end": 28.05,
   "text": "The work is never done. Over time, the couch stops feeling like *rest*."
  },
  {
   "start": 28.1,
   "end": 33.15,
   "text": "It feels like waiting in line. Nothing dramatic happens. That's the *cost*."
  },
  {
   "start": 33.2,
   "end": 41.05,
   "text": "Just a lot of evenings where Sam was present, but not really there. So what could he do instead?"
  }
